des $(8x+6y)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048604 :topic/id #uuid "ade9d1d5-3224-5403-9c8b-f3e5be0db3c5" :topic/math-academy-id 3080 :topic/title "Integer Divisibility"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba33ae8-ebcb-5138-8360-8827a4086e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453836} {:answer/id #uuid "456b6334-ff0e-5966-90f2-5c51a1ddd706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "456b6334-ff0e-5966-90f2-5c51a1ddd706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453837} :answer-field/id #uuid "fab1cedf-cc91-5eea-89d5-dcab0106295b" :answer-field/key "$6$ divides $(24x+30y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f842d8bd-31b0-5686-bfa3-548f19e273a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453838} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c01cf-3d68-5f93-8e43-8605005468a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c01cf-3d68-5f93-8e43-8605005468a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453839} :answer-field/id #uuid "2db380cf-aaea-5f16-9283-d7c95560d427" :answer-field/key "$3$ divides $(24x+30y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00534dc3-4006-5bef-9575-96f837e9a134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453840} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7abe4f-841c-5bd9-ae12-d42fe2195a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00534dc3-4006-5bef-9575-96f837e9a134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453840} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a3b668-b559-550b-9651-be66b31864e6" :answer-field/key "$5$ divides $(24x+30y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7df593d-9767-5ee4-9c1c-cf41d12d4aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-221932" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$6$ divides $(24x+30y)$” is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=6(4x+5y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+5y$ must be an integer, too. So, $6$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement “$3$ divides $(24x+30y)$” is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=3(8x+10y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $8x+10y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement “$5$ divides $(24x+30y)$” is false. For example, if $x=-1$ and $y=1,$ we have $24(-1)+30(1)=6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" “$6$ divides $(24x+30y)$” and “$3$ divides $(24x+30y)$” only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048574 :topic/id #uuid "aad2999b-dacb-527f-a4a8-1fce51919fe6" :topic/math-academy-id 4257 :topic/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc175e7-43f5-5dca-ae8c-fcffad9b5c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472826} {:answer/id #uuid "cd86dd80-446d-5040-befe-91f2357bee78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd86dd80-446d-5040-befe-91f2357bee78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472827} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a3cb157-cbd3-583d-b969-2172d9124ccd" :answer-field/key "If $x\\in Z$ then $-x\\in Z$, and if $-x\\in Z$ then $x\\in Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b3f2f24-9023-55b9-b00e-396cd842e16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472828} {:answer/id #uuid "b508a05d-6946-51ec-a146-08aa9e79dc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b508a05d-6946-51ec-a146-08aa9e79dc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472829} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ee6d34-66ed-5187-9e8e-9a460301418b" :answer-field/key "$x\\in Z$ is equivalent to $-x\\in Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a770702-80a6-5e1f-a0bc-32492cbf47be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472830} {:answer/id #uuid "66d4f2c5-b1fc-534a-84aa-8a2471983fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66d4f2c5-b1fc-534a-84aa-8a2471983fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472831} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e29e4e7-b6be-5e0d-8652-d55f8303b45a" :answer-field/key "$x\\in Z$ if and only if $-x\\in Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db5f04ef-3cc1-58de-87ac-cce7945d8e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-183355" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in Z.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\in Z.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in Z$ if and only if $-x\\in Z.$\n\n- $x\\in Z$ is equivalent to $-x\\in Z.$\n\n- If $x\\in Z$ then $-x\\in Z$, and if $-x\\in Z$ then $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $x\\in Z$ then $-x\\in Z$, and if $-x\\in Z$ then $x\\in Z.$”; “$x\\in Z$ is equivalent to $-x\\in Z.$”; “$x\\in Z$ if and only if $-x\\in Z.$”." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048574 :topic/id #uuid "aad2999b-dacb-527f-a4a8-1fce51919fe6" :topic/math-academy-id 4257 :topic/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates"} :activity/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407572} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407611} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048574 :topic/id #uuid "aad2999b-dacb-527f-a4a8-1fce51919fe6" :topic/math-academy-id 4257 :topic/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates"} :activity/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443904} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443913}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049459 :topic/id #uuid "f6fd4776-56f0-5112-9cdc-83e344004d93" :topic/math-academy-id 2131 :topic/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "755d214e-8d2a-5a21-b9cf-f0df0ddc65e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437406} {:answer/id #uuid "3bfd0671-10c2-5e45-a69d-18a97c5bcb8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "755d214e-8d2a-5a21-b9cf-f0df0ddc65e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437406} :answer-field/id #uuid "08fca85a-8f3f-5d04-ba2b-523fc3575ba4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6d7a93e-05d3-5b4e-a10d-309d06525f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437408} {:answer/id #uuid "cee06875-116c-5488-b531-455a557b12b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6d7a93e-05d3-5b4e-a10d-309d06525f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437408} :answer-field/id #uuid "77753f43-8be4-5002-8a52-0b36dbebd616" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0919152f-4318-5ee5-ab9e-853f1a97e081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437410} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd97fc8-8c06-56b4-a75e-62d1a96d9ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cd97fc8-8c06-56b4-a75e-62d1a96d9ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437411} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b9e3e64-ecdb-5c87-af06-d417e36b04d6" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438734} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98360c07-0eb0-5614-8178-f21e14480fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437412} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7d8c5d-3f07-50af-a145-77ac2e6077ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98360c07-0eb0-5614-8178-f21e14480fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437412} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a0366b6-425d-5c79-b027-f2d81a491b79" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2847820b-e13e-563d-bfbb-bab640514e5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105572" :question/problem "![](images/58/584016c88e5916984e181118d52caab95dba1fd0d861e0fd248a4e023d1b07da.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors decrease as we move horizontally and vertically towards the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a sink at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049459 :topic/id #uuid "f6fd4776-56f0-5112-9cdc-83e344004d93" :topic/math-academy-id 2131 :topic/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field"} :activity/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407612} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407635}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050743 :topic/id #uuid "62da5cd1-bbc7-584a-ba89-8e03cd9c311f" :topic/math-academy-id 252 :topic/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71f417cf-0536-54c4-b46a-510edd2f3084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472814} {:answer/id #uuid "74f27fa9-e14e-5a7b-a59d-e4f8f4f07523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71f417cf-0536-54c4-b46a-510edd2f3084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472814} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c82116e-ddf7-523c-8827-05efd60ca46b" :answer-field/key "If $-2\\notin Z,$ then $5$ is not prime." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb3e374-acff-5951-8e7b-106d3ee1d226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472816} {:answer/id #uuid "29aae364-4c1b-55ea-b0c7-3b01642bf4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fb3e374-acff-5951-8e7b-106d3ee1d226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472816} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6480a4-7991-54a8-8209-37a4015dd66a" :answer-field/key "If $5$ is prime, then $-2\\in Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473803} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dcb7e8d-cce0-53ff-95e0-c4e55ecc50af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472818} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9dc198-f0b8-5675-bee7-c3bb6d3fd1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c9dc198-f0b8-5675-bee7-c3bb6d3fd1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472819} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e90f976-19af-5624-afdd-dbae7aa38b78" :answer-field/key "If $5$ is not prime, then $-2\\notin Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23603376-708c-5de8-b4d0-019ec40ac31f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183340" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $-2\\in Z,$ **then** $5$ is prime.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement “If $-2\\notin Z,$ then $5$ is not prime” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If $5$ is prime, then $-2\\in Z.$” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If $5$ is not prime, then $-2\\notin Z.$” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $5$ is not prime, then $-2\\notin Z.$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050743 :topic/id #uuid "62da5cd1-bbc7-584a-ba89-8e03cd9c311f" :topic/math-academy-id 252 :topic/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive"} :activity/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407636} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407675}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050743 :topic/id #uuid "62da5cd1-bbc7-584a-ba89-8e03cd9c311f" :topic/math-academy-id 252 :topic/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "915545ce-c423-5da4-91dc-290407b53372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473446} {:answer/id #uuid "8f85f5bf-c4f5-5094-8323-a67c9fa53bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "915545ce-c423-5da4-91dc-290407b53372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473446} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898d384-3181-550c-8344-cde598e23fab" :answer-field/key "If you are not going to school, then you are sick." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3b76f77-9332-57a9-afde-de8d55488d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473448} {:answer/id #uuid "bee0a274-ed2c-5c01-b766-3ba728c9c822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3b76f77-9332-57a9-afde-de8d55488d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473448} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffea5c3f-a699-5852-afaa-150401a98451" :answer-field/key "If you are not sick, then you are going to school." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f64a71-8fa0-502d-8cc4-7ae6c1d1511b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473450} {:answer/id #uuid "80e07b43-5cc7-5ba7-bb18-f3644b44ddf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80e07b43-5cc7-5ba7-bb18-f3644b44ddf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473451} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a10d53-1347-54fd-b77a-a4d9ac2a0931" :answer-field/key "If you are going to school, then you are not sick." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41c661ac-cdce-5cf9-814b-cfcfe49d2399" :question/math-academy-id "q-82665" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** you are sick, **then** you are not going to school.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement “If you are not going to school, then you are sick” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If you are not sick, then you are going to school” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If you are going to school, then you are not sick” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If you are going to school, then you are not sick” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050743 :topic/id #uuid "62da5cd1-bbc7-584a-ba89-8e03cd9c311f" :topic/math-academy-id 252 :topic/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive"} :activity/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407636} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407672}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c3ee6-fd37-5cb0-b0ab-80e7a7cca090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454166} {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b613250-bfe0-5d10-933a-62b1f7c0e186" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454168} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8662e3-fc5d-5d99-afd6-2bc7152d04fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454168} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4d6e3a-1748-5dc1-aec5-5bf919354400" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6560a1-a8ef-5d21-8325-256e585e4826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454170} {:answer/id #uuid "7e317d01-b088-5a71-957d-334271a2bf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e6560a1-a8ef-5d21-8325-256e585e4826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454170} :answer-field/id #uuid "528428ad-5f38-5fd7-92de-7aab58b61f83" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5252a0f-1ef3-54ce-a8b5-332d495a5706" :question/math-academy-id "q-94782" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},\\text{ }{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent one, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution. Moreover, ${x}_{1}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nTherefore, from ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=-\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{2}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{2}$ can not be a linear combination of other vectors.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{3}$ can not be a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}.$ As a result ${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ can't be written as combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$ too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e67907b7-e5fc-55ed-b02e-f04b7649034e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472832} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac5139a-0ed3-5e4e-b49c-444e16cd16da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e67907b7-e5fc-55ed-b02e-f04b7649034e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472832} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ca68e3-cdcb-5115-9df3-5c384f137d37" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(y)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e15c7d-6886-5d43-a1d4-a913c7e4a2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472834} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d489d0-bbdf-56c9-87c9-a4dd8210ffdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9d489d0-bbdf-56c9-87c9-a4dd8210ffdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472835} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c5d54ab-2cf1-5535-92fe-67334161b71f" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(y)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5ae3570-9ffe-5221-809e-3dd6d305bbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472836} {:answer/id #uuid "b542d4a4-7ae3-596b-b54c-ae7b5ec35225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b542d4a4-7ae3-596b-b54c-ae7b5ec35225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472837} :answer-field/id #uuid "5679e407-6097-5abf-95a3-0053125f2381" :answer-field/key "$∀y\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(y).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25efa028-94e4-52c8-9fb8-df2dc5b08098" :question/math-academy-id "q-183509" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(y):$ $y<y+1⇒{y}^{-1}\\in Q.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set ${Z}^{-},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$y<y+1$\" is ${Z}^{-},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${y}^{-1}\\in Q$\" is ${Z}^{-}.$\n\nSince $A⇒B≡¬A∨B,$ the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\overset{―}{{Z}^{-}}\\cup {Z}^{-}=∅\\cup {Z}^{-}={Z}^{-}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(y)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(y)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}={Z}^{-}.$\n\n- Statement $∀y\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(y).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ coincides with the universal set, the statement $∀y\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(y)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(y)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$”; $∀y\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(y).$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"} :activity/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407780} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407818}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c12effc-0d2e-5f60-91b3-4b082defc75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473010} {:answer/id #uuid "db6f8ca9-f659-5482-bfbc-ac3d14292808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c12effc-0d2e-5f60-91b3-4b082defc75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473010} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac2a7ba8-a7d5-51bb-9737-2fb9badb547c" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(m)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd0196f9-2a31-51aa-978b-076eb83f731a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473012} {:answer/id #uuid "6cefa553-9147-584d-b52d-ba0b6c919c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cefa553-9147-584d-b52d-ba0b6c919c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473013} :answer-field/id #uuid "f20bcb74-e9de-5e43-9dff-893367804923" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(m)$ is ${2k:k\\in Z}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ace0e580-09a3-5a7c-ae03-3d96cd58410a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473014} {:answer/id #uuid "0554a362-f73e-52dd-acda-14d2788d4c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ace0e580-09a3-5a7c-ae03-3d96cd58410a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473014} :answer-field/id #uuid "a230043a-bfb8-5b6a-b5dc-5c9f0de766a1" :answer-field/key "$∀m\\in Z,\\,P(m).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "303b12dc-4682-5eea-846a-0e1ea50fc6ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-216465" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(m):$ $\\frac{m}{2}$ is an integer\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{m}{2}$ is an integer if and only if $m$ is even, we have that the truth set of our predicate is ${T}_{P}={2k:k\\in Z}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(m)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(m)$ is ${2k:k\\in Z}.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}={2k:k\\in Z}.$\n\n- Statement $∀m\\in Z,\\,P(m).$ is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ doesn't coincide with the universal set, the statement $∀m\\in Z,\\,P(m)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(m)$ is ${2k:k\\in Z}.$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"} :activity/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407780} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407819}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33eb7a72-fa8b-50b1-8ebc-aa7cd26028d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453788} {:answer/id #uuid "3f148267-ad3c-5618-bf40-bc705ab3bdfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33eb7a72-fa8b-50b1-8ebc-aa7cd26028d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/