kbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473815} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3b2f22-6930-528a-8709-74fb24f79384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472842} {:answer/id #uuid "057da9f1-a7a7-55f3-89d1-becde4fe4af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "057da9f1-a7a7-55f3-89d1-becde4fe4af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472843} :answer-field/id #uuid "3382a728-8dac-58e5-b18b-2b9a83affe0c" :answer-field/key "$∃n\\in N,\\,P(n).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ab7419f-dd45-5016-a048-0ef13ef60278" :question/math-academy-id "q-183552" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(n):$ ${n}^{2}\\in N$ and $n+5>1$ \n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $N,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"${n}^{2}\\in N$\" is the set $N,$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"$n+5>1$\" is $N.$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=N\\cap N=N.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(n)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(n)$ is $N.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=N.$\n\n- Statement $∃n\\in N,\\,P(n).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃n\\in N,\\,P(n)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(n)$ is $N.$”; $∃n\\in N,\\,P(n).$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"} :activity/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407780} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407816}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c4d527-5e01-5264-8001-c16ba5c829f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453880} {:answer/id #uuid "8a788be2-6daa-5a9a-b61f-b090c8b8cf80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a788be2-6daa-5a9a-b61f-b090c8b8cf80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453881} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d46ebdc-4ea8-5b5d-a791-12ebf82b2b2b" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7662fdd-d050-5004-a857-2d86c30b4a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453882} {:answer/id #uuid "9233290a-d139-5d2d-91b5-3115178cf2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7662fdd-d050-5004-a857-2d86c30b4a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9a1015-1583-5e39-b729-2685f362e667" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $-1$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f5a5f0-e3d5-58cb-a9a2-e0e244128177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453884} {:answer/id #uuid "6013b3d6-d8f8-5f12-8351-83ccb30ce208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f5a5f0-e3d5-58cb-a9a2-e0e244128177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453884} :answer-field/id #uuid "81040326-5134-5a42-8539-aac88ecd9a5e" :answer-field/key "The limit exists and is equal to $\\frac{1}{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36139" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $-1$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2}$” is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=-{x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2(-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit exists and is equal to $\\frac{1}{3}$” is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407821} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407852}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e09de5d-566b-53b7-938e-4cd69784f908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453162} {:answer/id #uuid "09739bfe-5ef1-5a91-a5aa-5281c92dda9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e09de5d-566b-53b7-938e-4cd69784f908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453162} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d5a350-84ff-5946-86f2-1d19d8d7220c" :answer-field/key "$f(-2)=f(4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cee3daa-3190-55b4-a76d-c60b5757491d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453164} {:answer/id #uuid "f84f942c-6e9f-5b7c-af7b-f2c81298fce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84f942c-6e9f-5b7c-af7b-f2c81298fce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453165} :answer-field/id #uuid "631b3c6b-1149-5d42-a891-5e829966c88f" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53fda273-36a0-5e47-98ef-2cc2874bb65a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453166} {:answer/id #uuid "747834de-2a79-5887-b0c3-1e01bf258a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "747834de-2a79-5887-b0c3-1e01bf258a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453167} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae9ece0-8770-5aea-a183-8518985dc8d5" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a3dbd42-cd16-5083-8842-33f0028feb3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105207" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,4]\\to [-3,9]$ which is given by $f(x)=2x+1?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd931a87d6a5fb32d10ed931f443a8175f0760eba9fe2fe69336f8f79e9fd68.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-2)=f(4)$ is false. We have $f(2)=2(-2)+1=-3$ and $f(4)=2\\cdot 4+1=9.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[-2,4]$ that map to the same element in $[-3,9].$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is an injection” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"} :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407855} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407892}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d35f4e88-6bef-5641-80a0-028f685e3519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472466} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3f2a4a-cd53-59d2-a981-e675cff4a3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd3f2a4a-cd53-59d2-a981-e675cff4a3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472467} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0534f15-2962-5ddb-8f73-7a2f2475c0f6" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2x+3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b312ff-ce3e-5e32-9aeb-756e89a5f671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472468} {:answer/id #uuid "258df532-e4f2-5710-b640-abc2180b4c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19b312ff-ce3e-5e32-9aeb-756e89a5f671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472468} :answer-field/id #uuid "29f20d63-79e9-56ff-8e1e-a8b4a6fa0751" :answer-field/key "$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=(x-2)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc08267-7ffc-5f21-aad1-afa99e374adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472470} {:answer/id #uuid "b144395e-d1f5-57f9-9d59-546422f9a22d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc08267-7ffc-5f21-aad1-afa99e374adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472470} :answer-field/id #uuid "09886aba-2044-5edb-a629-02c3209ba59e" :answer-field/key "$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23e55f80-c083-57f4-820d-7aa2d67256ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-105210" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2x+3$” is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3 & =2{x}_{2}+3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- “$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=(x-2)^{2}$” is *not*  an injection.  For example, $g(1)=1=g(3),$ but $1\\ne 3.$\n\n- “$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$” is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2\\pi ),$ but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2x+3$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"} :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407855} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407894}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bed8e09f-6511-5608-ad7f-00fed5f7d006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473422} {:answer/id #uuid "0660c018-03e7-593b-893d-7b3d19276164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0660c018-03e7-593b-893d-7b3d19276164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473423} :answer-field/id #uuid "892f7afd-5416-5113-aefe-704db7f8e832" :answer-field/key "$f(-3)=f(3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7a5268-1ea4-5698-9778-5ff94d592124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473424} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb9c785-7c45-5b99-abc3-5f2d6190191d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd7a5268-1ea4-5698-9778-5ff94d592124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473424} :answer-field/id #uuid "e62134da-b3ae-5a4f-9cc3-bd3538e36744" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-3,3],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8e433b6-43ce-5e1b-a7c8-ad9306558803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473426} {:answer/id #uuid "ac914ea6-d76c-5ffe-bcd2-cdb587ee9678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8e433b6-43ce-5e1b-a7c8-ad9306558803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473426} :answer-field/id #uuid "77db2363-4339-5281-bb25-6dd26c42fa43" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c2e3f55-ea9b-5b9e-badf-26b9e5d93c01" :question/math-academy-id "q-80384" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0a08488ba59344033205903ca973870d0b10837295ced970bf307342e6f7241.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-3,3]\\to [-3,0]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-3)=f(3)$ is true. According to the graph, we have $f(-3)=f(3)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-3,3],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. Again, we have $f(-3)=f(3)$ but $-3\\ne 3.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-3,3],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-3,3],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(-3)=f(3)$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"} :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407855} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407891}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2c29d1e-6a71-5a2b-9207-175266e9f0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473416} {:answer/id #uuid "ad465e70-567d-5d4c-b486-b4b289256ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2c29d1e-6a71-5a2b-9207-175266e9f0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473416} :answer-field/id #uuid "8acda064-7e39-560e-a976-7d967bc557bc" :answer-field/key "$f(0)=f(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc875d8-5208-5b0d-a170-d502605bcd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473418} {:answer/id #uuid "d55f5921-9bdf-51a5-9635-da02ad1b37fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d55f5921-9bdf-51a5-9635-da02ad1b37fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473419} :answer-field/id #uuid "13e0236f-cc20-53bb-b712-8b098c3617d4" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "345cdf7e-550b-5e3d-b83b-320d18379e78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473420} {:answer/id #uuid "696eeb35-6a02-5604-8e86-344ab522fba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "696eeb35-6a02-5604-8e86-344ab522fba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473421} :answer-field/id #uuid "90f68307-4853-500d-b43e-b3e760f1eca0" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58fa3eda-7303-530c-b266-fd43b4b16a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80370" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c2f22af3b39c28d885ac490aae190e1b2d4ad55828a552fec031069d6d912a2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(0)=f(1)$ is false. According to the graph, we have $f(0)=0$ and $f(1)=1.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is **one-to-one**” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"} :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407855} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407890}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048532 :topic/id #uuid "a7907bdb-038e-5baa-a4ae-df7b362e291b" :topic/math-academy-id 4100 :topic/title "Continuous Random Variables Over Infinite Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abd3b4ad-7245-5359-aa08-f555f6155e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453466} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa7c36-5307-50a0-bf63-41b72cb111a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa7c36-5307-50a0-bf63-41b72cb111a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453467} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ace91eb-339b-5d50-a799-7b88dbafe125" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d15f02a2-e02d-5286-a449-4115be4fc330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453468} {:answer/id #uuid "81e8d8a3-4012-5902-b1fd-cd50cc9744af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e8d8a3-4012-5902-b1fd-cd50cc9744af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453469} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f2197b0-eada-5d24-bd2b-fe0d8b2c6994" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "305dbab8-5c7a-5858-b8d4-92e8c2368110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453470} {:answer/id #uuid "ab13c02c-2738-5b13-ae31-2638c7d3c679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab13c02c-2738-5b13-ae31-2638c7d3c679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453471} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c2b331-d72c-5f5c-8d12-1798339f28ae" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b46ac655-a97e-50cb-a022-2af841ed15e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160451" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is true. Since statements “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” and ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$”; ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$; “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a264b855-1904-5164-bede-a3a58bf8a87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473344} {:answer/id #uuid "76849f48-b02a-51c8-ab54-bc3cea4dc51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76849f48-b02a-51c8-ab54-bc3cea4dc51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473345} :answer-field/id #uuid "65d6b9db-5cf9-5d84-a615-3117e641ebb8" :answer-field/key "$n=9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96047d36-a564-5410-a080-0f5ee960c506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473346} {:answer/id #uuid "21ca83ec-352e-5cd0-8ac7-bbcc21f9368c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96047d36-a564-5410-a080-0f5ee960c506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473346} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e78b1e-a0f9-5ef4-8159-54dc686fe017" :answer-field/key "$n=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "577ef78e-2229-5fcf-aacf-90f73efb2e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473348} {:answer/id #uuid "9895344f-eccd-5c07-97f0-80c877ad5005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9895344f-eccd-5c07-97f0-80c877ad5005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473349} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fa22280-2abd-5607-b207-841f7d4a254b" :answer-field/key "$n=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ce0c9ed-8f49-5909-b44d-93bd60aa3e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76964" :question/problem "Given that $26≡8\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=26-8=18.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $9∣18$ because $18÷9=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\n- Note that $8∤18.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $3∣18$ because $18÷3=6,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $n=9$; $n=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3b57aa-3f05-58d8-8630-4c61e4a9f20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472448} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b42f5c-a47b-5d87-955d-4192d359f4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4b42f5c-a47b-5d87-955d-4192d359f4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472449} :answer-field/id #uuid "8654bd37-45a7-5eeb-8f75-3aaf4ab3c1de" :answer-field/key "$n=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0fe676-ef48-52fb-bbb8-2688d64b0a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472450} {:answer/id #uuid "15f5daec-6f1d-5882-8490-35e7cd0b95e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d0fe676-ef48-52fb-bbb8-2688d64b0a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472450} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b201d2d-d239-519c-8c8d-abf23fc895a8" :answer-field/key "$n=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473620} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058504a0-749e-5beb-ac08-186e01df798f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472452} {:answer/id #uuid "de40d40f-81da-54bb-ad0b-467f017ba4e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de40d40f-81da-54bb-ad0b-467f017ba4e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472453} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad59f688-ccde-5029-8b8f-da7752bcaf1f" :answer-field/key "$n=9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c433443-9a9c-5d0b-84b5-bc247b100915" :question/math-academy-id "q-103390" :question/problem "Given that $29≡-16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=29-(-16)=45.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $5∣45$ because $45÷5=9,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=5.$\n\n- Note that $8∤45.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $9∣45$ because $45÷9=5,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $n=5$; $n=9$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "398716c2-d0e6-5106-a702-2f71d957726f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Integers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d490cf1-d662-56a2-8631-21d543f11c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453120} {:answer/id #uuid "ce480cda-9021-5f06-a8cd-b9ca16301c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d490cf1-d662-56a2-8631-21d543f11c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453120} :answer-field/id #uuid "af1230fc-88f6-56f0-a44f-a2580bb43a87" :answer-field/key "$11≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5f14a7e-4460-5c56-88cd-b67e7eb770b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453122} {:answer/id #uuid "168ce81c-a8ca-550c-ae67-a01761495d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5f14a7e-4460-5c56-88cd-b67e7eb770b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453122} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b1c902-2a3c-5a5a-8275-9ced53169a21" :answer-field/key "$18≡16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9917c881-2ee9-5be2-b248-f90217ecd423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453124} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8e630-8f3b-5355-ac11-368a8e967b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8e630-8f3b-5355-ac11-368a8e967b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453125} :answer-field/id #uuid "0490fa62-dcfa-5271-a176-054c103e687c" :answer-field/key "$24≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a4a4ae5-eba9-597a-b12c-2ce503fbc86a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103385" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Case $11≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$ gives a false statement because $3∤(11-3).$ Notice that $11-3=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Case $18≡16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ gives a false statement because $4∤(18-16).$ Notice that $18-16=2,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Case $24≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ gives a true statement. Indeed, $5∣(24-19).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(24-19)÷5=5÷5=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $24≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] 