er-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b17c24c5-e750-5126-8785-6318018ca783" :question/math-academy-id "q-76959" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-5≡11\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$ is false because $3∤(-5-11).$ Notice that $-5-11=-16,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement $-7≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ is true because $7\\,|\\,(-7-0).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-0)÷7=-7÷7=-7\n$$\n\n- Statement $6≡25\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ is false because $9∤(6-25).$ Notice that $6-25=-19,$ which is not divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-7≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42708017-2e08-541a-a0c3-70b49941a5a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472442} {:answer/id #uuid "e796520e-fbe7-52e2-88bd-0591456c7db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e796520e-fbe7-52e2-88bd-0591456c7db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472443} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b8daba-48cf-53e7-bdcb-854ca7473f00" :answer-field/key "$n=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2fcceb-6977-5edc-b972-6ef48acdf27f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472444} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a188cf-5a7a-50fd-aea8-3c7c08b142c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a188cf-5a7a-50fd-aea8-3c7c08b142c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472445} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c6d071-eb27-5b7d-8267-405e1cf6365a" :answer-field/key "$n=6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473617} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "686ee57d-c0d8-5367-a4e4-b83dca7772e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472446} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0a5473-9207-5805-87cb-d995d33d62f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a0a5473-9207-5805-87cb-d995d33d62f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472447} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a676e29-3d72-5aed-abaf-a3b3398036a5" :answer-field/key "$n=9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e77d765e-3b79-5534-bec0-79f592cc8d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103387" :question/problem "Given that $-3≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-3-15=-18.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣(-18)$ because $(-18)÷2=-9,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $6∣(-18)$ because $(-18)÷6=-3,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=6.$\n\n- Note that $9∣(-18)$ because $(-18)÷9=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $n=2$; $n=6$; $n=9$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2cb28a0-b456-55cc-94c3-2a35edde21be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Integers are Coprime" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048141 :topic/id #uuid "82ca0e31-666b-5e06-8d65-c724c2ffa4fb" :topic/math-academy-id 2676 :topic/title "The Euclidean Algorithm"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16764622-cd26-55e1-8a5a-7e55b57682c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454286} {:answer/id #uuid "ba98f67b-67c0-5060-a532-9100f74d628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba98f67b-67c0-5060-a532-9100f74d628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454287} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d2efd04-ce36-5615-b920-a167a18c5522" :answer-field/key "$\\text{gcd}(765,221)=17$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f64992-3a27-5317-b1d1-b10093213230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454288} {:answer/id #uuid "ede5a4d3-58f8-507f-ae2f-d2870f910272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83f64992-3a27-5317-b1d1-b10093213230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454288} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ae289e-e270-51af-ae40-76298154f43a" :answer-field/key "$\\text{gcd}(765,221)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a8cbab-7fe7-5051-b478-b3b6fcd97579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454290} {:answer/id #uuid "647bb829-b1ad-502f-ac68-5b6629e48201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a8cbab-7fe7-5051-b478-b3b6fcd97579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454290} :answer-field/id #uuid "d885f16a-81d5-5090-9f2d-2ec0e5cb9bd6" :answer-field/key "$765$ and $221$ are coprime" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3936dcf8-3c18-5d25-b1ef-fee251049b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-98480" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that two integers are coprime if their greatest common divisor is $1.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{gcd}(765,221)=17$ is true, while statement $\\text{gcd}(765,221)=1$ is false. Indeed, let's use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}765 & = & 221\\cdot 3 & + & 102 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 221 & = & 102\\cdot 2 & + & 17 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 102 & = & 17\\cdot 6 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $17.$ So, the greatest common divisor of $765$ and $221$ is $17:$\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(765,221)=17.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$765$ and $221$ are coprime” is false. Since $\\text{gcd}(765,221)>1,$ the numbers are not coprime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{gcd}(765,221)=17$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2cb28a0-b456-55cc-94c3-2a35edde21be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Integers are Coprime" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048141 :topic/id #uuid "82ca0e31-666b-5e06-8d65-c724c2ffa4fb" :topic/math-academy-id 2676 :topic/title "The Euclidean Algorithm"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db731a1-a78b-5cb1-a275-94cbe9841b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454280} {:answer/id #uuid "20717d2e-b744-557d-ad03-8171eb0fe0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20717d2e-b744-557d-ad03-8171eb0fe0ad" :answer/type {:db/id 