#edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3d9c034-c1fd-5d1f-ba8a-08e4030e4374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574259} {:answer/id #uuid "247bb068-cfea-56a1-aa73-1a29a0c03c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3d9c034-c1fd-5d1f-ba8a-08e4030e4374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574259} :answer-field/id #uuid "6554548e-d8d0-5d0f-8f34-11d92408528a" :answer-field/key "Column 5: $\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcd1cb26-1c44-5d74-aa8e-2093ab435f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-130950" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"} :activity/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410764} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410773} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"} :activity/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572820} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573353}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2fffb5d-3a48-5bb6-ac88-ce930684ca97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473434} {:answer/id #uuid "294eeec8-975d-5c82-ae0f-2771583b8dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "294eeec8-975d-5c82-ae0f-2771583b8dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473435} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd849a69-1d9a-56c7-b5dd-51c95b3a7fb1" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474112} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840247a1-44e4-5764-9cf1-c049a173b2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473436} {:answer/id #uuid "946cdfda-8e89-55b0-9fa0-8e85f564674b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "946cdfda-8e89-55b0-9fa0-8e85f564674b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473437} :answer-field/id #uuid "73a56616-2123-5fa5-b737-ce96e6534c3c" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba3e6678-4e3d-5c51-a908-8193a93dce9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473438} {:answer/id #uuid "2fed4611-09f6-5910-ade6-a7e1facbbba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fed4611-09f6-5910-ade6-a7e1facbbba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473439} :answer-field/id #uuid "2124b191-2881-520e-896a-bfc3832d55f9" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00868f73-2a29-5bc5-b5fa-287f2fcfd175" :question/math-academy-id "q-82304" :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef3933fc56e981bd0ef6e88754c46f5ab00b15230cce5fc2ea224ecf7c1f8f0e.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2\\sqrt[3]{x}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/f0/f020379f306770bd87fc499ac1fef238dc6aa639fb36d5229502fcd7dd455610.png)\n\n        \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ will cover the entire interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is true because the function is both surjective and injective.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection”; “The function is a surjection”; “The function is a bijection”." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"} :activity/title "Bijections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410903} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410940}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e829b3-51c9-553b-9a85-45a365a040d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472772} {:answer/id #uuid "25d4d0b8-e87c-5870-9268-7bd36f45c2be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e829b3-51c9-553b-9a85-45a365a040d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472772} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab2f2b46-2c6e-5eb1-85c3-ad99eab4b5bb" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b76c9ff3-fe58-5372-b648-22e1105f9edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472774} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0aa8d4-59ff-53f5-b71d-5399b2d3aa82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc0aa8d4-59ff-53f5-b71d-5399b2d3aa82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472775} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3d2d3d-6e53-548d-8c99-3c996253ee94" :answer-field/key "$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7d6de4-ec23-5a7c-93c0-50dd18473fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472776} {:answer/id #uuid "2f38aaba-83e0-5b28-9931-c911d3ca9a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7d6de4-ec23-5a7c-93c0-50dd18473fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472776} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e1483-33f9-5dc2-81fd-fee7d86b3dcf" :answer-field/key "$h:Z\\to Z$ defined by $h(x)=2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f4dc780-0892-5640-8a66-1c76dbdf69ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-170667" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This means that \n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, for example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=4.$\n\n- “$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=2x$” is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in R,$ we can choose an $x\\in R$ such that $g(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =y \\\\ 2x & =y \\\\ x & =\\frac{y}{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that\n\n$$\ng(x)=g(\\frac{y}{2})=2(\\frac{y}{2})=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $g$ is both surjective and injective, $g$ is bijective.\n\n- “$h:Z\\to Z$ defined by $h(x)=2x$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Notice that if $x$ is an integer number, then $h(x)=2x$ is an even number. This means that the range of $h$ is the set of even numbers.\nSo, for example, there is no value $x\\in Z$ such that $h(x)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=2x$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"} :activity/title "Bijections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410903} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410941}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46ba97c8-22ce-5f2e-a361-5e8cdc04dd4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472484} {:answer/id #uuid "b27c6df3-9636-5cec-a7c6-7e29c522a025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b27c6df3-9636-5cec-a7c6-7e29c522a025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472485} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb62bcbf-8eae-5cf3-b5ae-4a506ba9980e" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa5400a8-4d69-5498-bb26-cf35113f0a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472486} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a7df63-ed8d-5f4d-8c4c-c2ea8c9ec5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3a7df63-ed8d-5f4d-8c4c-c2ea8c9ec5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472487} :answer-field/id #uuid "08bfc292-3bc3-54f3-9448-43fbcbae4c11" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc48bae5-5a50-5365-8135-13ed7b0935d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472488} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d6054e-cf6e-54d1-a1b7-c5a2fedc0e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8d6054e-cf6e-54d1-a1b7-c5a2fedc0e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472489} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b1b7116-3a54-5f89-a498-e625b68c4215" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80ecff06-aa66-5d3f-b38e-164bc959ec2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105321" :question/problem "![](images/63/63032bf65ec10d55f9a0b968a7179db934ad6f17b869d50999e4a0f710be9977.png)\n\nFor the function $f:(-1,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/71/71bd13b2dd618fb60cd2e7f6c2e3807f3449e233ccb9b60e1cbd14cc928345b3.png)\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is true because the function is both surjective and injective.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection”; “The function is a surjection”; “The function is a bijection”." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"} :activity/title "Bijections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410903} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410943}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e823525c-d068-59c5-b79c-15a3ccf71c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473362} {:answer/id #uuid "891e6926-8a5d-5e45-a792-62f1489010a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891e6926-8a5d-5e45-a792-62f1489010a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473363} :answer-field/id #uuid "19b384f0-5c30-5d34-9679-cd7e07ed517c" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0389deac-290e-5e2b-a79a-47bb5723e7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473364} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a48bf-eee6-5f4b-abad-5b2daa66506b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0389deac-290e-5e2b-a79a-47bb5723e7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473364} :answer-field/id #uuid "410ca3ae-a20d-51b7-85fe-4743d9e9e5fd" :answer-field/key "$g:Q\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d7f5c0-1fd8-56a4-9076-f3007ffc482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473366} {:answer/id #uuid "25dd17ba-ad09-5a8f-ab00-e55bf3b14ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d7f5c0-1fd8-56a4-9076-f3007ffc482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473366} :answer-field/id #uuid "c95d975f-eefe-5a67-a299-22eea80c5b71" :answer-field/key "$h:Z\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)={2}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f181e810-d779-5077-8c9b-e3a1b446edcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-77480" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=x+1$” is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in R,$ we can choose an $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =y \\\\ x+1 & =y \\\\ x & =y-1\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that, \n\n$$\nf(x)=f(y-1)=(y-1)+1=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}+1 & ={x}_{2}+1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is both surjective and injective, $f$ is bijective.    \n\n- “$g:Q\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. As a counterexample, choose $y=2.$ Then there is no rational number $x$  such that $g(x)=2.$ The only numbers $x$ that satisfies ${x}^{2}=2$ are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$\n\n- “$h:Z\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)={2}^{x}$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. As a counterexample, choose $y=0.$ Then there is no integer $x$  such that $g(x)=0,$  because ${2}^{x}>0$ for all $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=x+1$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"} :activity/title "Bijections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410903} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410939}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac4098b-5192-54c8-8f6d-e195dab81971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473440} {:answer/id #uuid "41e127f3-fa89-57cb-ad00-c33a0ad41569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e127f3-fa89-57cb-ad00-c33a0ad41569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473441} :answer-field/id #uuid "2de55556-81c5-5e7d-8e52-b17b07e64f9e" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d987b394-ce7e-50ee-bd9e-15b2865507e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473442} {:answer/id #uuid "b94f447a-92fa-59ce-915e-6bc43de8b1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d987b394-ce7e-50ee-bd9e-15b2865507e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473442} :answer-field/id #uuid "18762654-245a-5a4b-9f7e-5b1cdc56bc3f" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "594452de-a12a-52ba-853d-a92da8d4b8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473444} {:answer/id #uuid "af604334-e529-5439-bf59-b34bae36264b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "594452de-a12a-52ba-853d-a92da8d4b8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473444} :answer-field/id #uuid "68b84854-48a5-5f9e-bc3e-762fc29560f5" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f636c031-3e1e-5fb8-bd29-acadcf4da72e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82572" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce68b2f27b88bd43d6eebfa5380a22c00e15e4194e0ad45e6778f761667a3ceb.png)\n\nFor the function $f:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=x-2$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/2f/2ff4c0183b91aa23d780f665aa0f038b374583e9f24e245951c4c69ea5f2e5b8.png)\n\n           \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. There is no value $x$ for which $f(x)=-2\\in R.$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\n Therefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"} :activity/title "Bijections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410903} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410942}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049805 :topic/id #uuid "155403ed-fbfa-59a9-b928-e762a73145ef" :topic/math-academy-id 247 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e80d5d8d-2b17-5886-9b55-a7b81e348575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453622} {:answer/id #uuid "eb698ee6-4b77-5b14-90cb-e74df6b1abac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb698ee6-4b77-5b14-90cb-e74df6b1abac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453623} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab0edef-ad32-52ce-a777-7ef518d62f83" :answer-field/key "$A⇒B≡¬A∨B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8de87b1-d8ef-50e0-94f7-a2832adb4959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453624} {:answer/id #uuid "f7312739-063d-5aef-8534-6f2ac7974c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8de87b1-d8ef-50e0-94f7-a2832adb4959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453624} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9edf5f2-ac8c-5b69-99b2-3ae4c084b126" :answer-field/key "$¬(A⇒B)≡A∨¬B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54641cb5-3584-597c-bcb0-67da0251b5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453626} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7d916c-501c-57d8-ad96-61e5a1dc8fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a7d916c-501c-57d8-ad96-61e5a1dc8fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453627} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2b4fa69-fdf7-5386-8328-31ecb2099e55" :answer-field/key "$¬(A⇒B)≡A∧¬B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7ec246a-1c3b-5830-ae08-ed99cbcc20da" :question/math-academy-id "q-182503" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement $A⇒B≡¬A∨B$ is true. Indeed, $A⇒B$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬A∨B.$\n\n- Statement $¬(A⇒B)≡A∧¬B$ is true, while statement $¬(A⇒B)≡A∨¬B$ is false. From part $A⇒B≡¬A∨B$, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\nA⇒B≡¬A∨B\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(A⇒B)≡¬(¬A∨B).\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∨B)≡¬(¬A)∧¬B.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nA∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(A⇒B)$ is equivalent to $A∧¬B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A⇒B≡¬A∨B$; $¬(A⇒B)≡A∧¬B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050777 :topic/id #uuid "65e4f73e-43a8-5089-914d-135e7396b995" :topic/math-academy-id 2821 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff3ba28-38e8-51bc-a126-2eff2903bff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472574} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8239a8-397c-5bf4-8f09-ac6412a0e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8239a8-397c-5bf4-8f09-ac6412a0e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d4328ce-d94c-50ad-9bc6-66e180d0c379" :answer-field/key "$¬Q∧(P∨Q)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de4aeae3-2eea-55f8-9d3b-f6f28669d75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472576} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb9487c-635d-5949-9980-a665c9ff96ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffb9487c-635d-5949-9980-a665c9ff96ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472577} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b67704-7d9c-5f26-8cd4-1364e0247ba7" :answer-field/key "$P∧¬Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "428e1b82-e6da-5eab-9b6a-0c2af131b494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472578} {:answer/id #uuid "d54291b6-7ef2-55e0-96fb-76e1195bcd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "428e1b82-e6da-5eab-9b6a-0c2af131b494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472578} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa69a530-25df-51d2-8915-d0fef8fbe9e6" :answer-field/key "$¬P∧¬Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8076c0f-174e-5d1d-bedf-553b0bcc1d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-127969" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q∧(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∧¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$ and $P∧¬Q$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$; $P∧¬Q$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050777 :topic/id #uuid "65e4f73e-43a8-5089-914d-135e7396b995" :topic/math-academy-id 2821 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence"} :activity/title "Logical Equivalence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420440} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420442}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048819 :topic/id #uuid "c29ac9c3-f2c1-572b-9251-f82101c5a30e" :topic/math-academy-id 1375 :topic/title "The Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of a 2x2 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9114a1-aa7f-5df3-814e-651d0530d5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473326} {:answer/id #uuid "032cba6f-622b-5534-9122-a6d2e0064c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9114a1-aa7f-5df3-814e-651d0530d5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473326} :answer-field/id #uuid "86c73323-d68f-52e7-bb08-f5a7c5c876ad" :answer-field/key "$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ef3ca8-ce71-5b0e-9160-127af09d7f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473328} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7e1916-223f-548d-9df4-0fcfee646ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20ef3ca8-ce71-5b0e-9160-127af09d7f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473328} :answer-field/id #uuid "55a5184c-a43a-5418-856c-b2919b5f0f7f" :answer-field/key "$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b23bec9-7f3a-5e08-adee-f648ba08bc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473330} {:answer/id #uuid "c58c188c-bab8-504b-94fd-1ab2f97a5ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c58c188c-bab8-504b-94fd-1ab2f97a5ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473331} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c1a60f6-a246-55e5-8725-fa3150b13681" :answer-field/key "If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3,$ then $2v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ddf6872-c9fc-59bb-a8a4-f3c287d11e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75724" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-1$ (but not $1$).\n\n- Statement “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5.$” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{v}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-4{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=-4v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-4$ (but not $5$).\n\n- Statement “If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3,$ then $2v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-3.$” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(2v)=2Av=2(-3v)=-3(2v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(2v)=-3(2v),$ and $2v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $2v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-3.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3,$ then $2v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-3.$” only."}]
